**** Changes from 2026.10.13 (riesmeier)

- Updated information on latest CMake version:
  Changed latest CMake version that was tested to 4.4.4.
  Affects: CMakeLists.txt

**** Changes from 2026.10.11 (eichelberg)

- Correctly print cert validity dates after 2049:
  OpenSSL represents certificate validity dates in 2050 or later using the
  GENERALIZEDTIME format, as required by RFC 5280. Such dates were simply
  not printed at all. This is now fixed.
  Thanks to Roberto Locatelli for the bug report and fix.
  Affects: dcmsign/libsrc/sicert.cc
           dcmtls/libsrc/tlslayer.cc

**** Changes from 2026.10.09 (sunderland)

- Added support for Label Map Segment. to TID 1411:
  The "Referenced Segment" content item of TID 1411 (Volumetric ROI
  Measurements) only accepted Segmentation Storage and Surface
  Segmentation Storage objects. Now, the check uses
  DSRImageReferenceValue::isSegmentation(), so that Label Map Segmentation
  Storage objects (and all other segmentation SOP classes known to this
  method) are accepted as well.
  Extended the TID 1500 test accordingly: a label map segmentation is
  accepted, both as a reference value and as a dataset, while an image is
  rejected with CMR_EC_InvalidSegmentationObject.
  Thanks to GitHub user "Sunderlandkyl" (Kyle Sunderland) for the pull
  request.
  This closes GitHub PR #161.
  Affects: dcmsr/libcmr/tid1411.cc
           dcmsr/tests/tsrcmr.cc

**** Changes from 2026.10.09 (eichelberg)

- Improved man page:
  Thanks to Mathieu Malaterre for the suggestion.
  Affects: dcmdata/docs/img2dcm.man

**** Changes from 2026.09.28 (eichelberg)

- Fixed build on NetBSD.
  Affects: dcmpstat/tests/tests.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.22 (onken)

- Fixed race between the publish jobs on GitHub:
  ci_addons moved the "latest" tag via a temporary tag "latest-tmp".
  A publish job of another platform that fetched the tags in that moment
  mistook "latest-tmp" for a release tag and created a regular release
  with that name. The "latest" tag is now moved with a single forced
  update of the ref instead.
  Affects: .github/workflows/cmake-linux.yml
           .github/workflows/cmake-mac.yml
           .github/workflows/cmake-win.yml

- Added 32-bit build to Windows "latest" workflow:
  The Windows workflow now builds x64 and Win32 as a matrix using the
  respective 3.7.0 support packages and publishes both zip packages
  (dcmtk-*-win64.zip, dcmtk-*-win32.zip) in a single publish step.
  The build uses a matrix build, i.e. a runner is executed vor every
  "combination" we provide (in this case for Windows only 32 bit and
  64 bit, not different compilers or Windows versions). This allows
  re-use of most of the existing YAML code for both runs.
  Affects: .github/workflows/cmake-win.yml

- Added OpenSSL DLLs to Windows "latest" package:
  The Windows "latest" GitHub package provides OpenSSL as DLLs, which the
  CMake INSTALL target does not pick up. Tools loading dcmtls, dcmdsig or
  dcmpstat therefore failed to start from the GitHub snapshot builds.
  This patch ensures the related OpenSSL libs are copied to the output
  package as well before it gets zipped up.
  Affects: .github/workflows/cmake-win.yml

