**** Changes from 2026.09.20 (onken)

- Regenerated dependencies.
  Affects: dcmiod/libsrc/Makefile.dep
           dcmiod/tests/Makefile.dep
           dcmpstat/tests/Makefile.dep

- Fixed rounding of CIELab/RGB conversion in dcmpstat:
  DVPSGraphicLayer truncated instead of rounded when converting RGB to
  DICOM CIELab and back, causing an off-by-one error in about half of
  all values; out-of-range values would have wrapped around.
  - Results are now rounded to nearest and clamped to 0..65535.
  - Added unit test module for dcmpstat covering the recommended
    display value handling of DVPSGraphicLayer (retired RGB value on
    read, CIELab round trip, grayscale fallback).
  Added:   dcmpstat/tests/tests.cc
           dcmpstat/tests/tgl.cc
  Affects: dcmpstat/libsrc/dvpsgl.cc
           dcmpstat/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmpstat/tests/Makefile.in

- Aligned CIELab conversion with the ICC PCS (D50):
  DICOM (part 3) stores Recommended Display CIELab Values as PCS-Values,
  i.e. encoded like the ICC Profile Connection Space, and the reference
  white of the PCS is D50 (ICC.1). IODCIELabUtil computed CIELab relative
  to D65 (the sRGB white point) instead, yielding slightly wrong a*/b*
  values for chromatic colors. The conversion now follows the updated
  PixelMed implementation (see dcmqi issue #563), so that both toolkits
  yield consistent results.
  - sRGB -> linear RGB -> CIE XYZ (D65) -> Bradford adaptation to D50
    -> CIELab, using the matrices and constants of the CSS Color Module
    Level 4 sample code. CIEXYZ values of the class API are now D50
    (PCS) values.
  - Colors outside the sRGB gamut are clipped per channel instead of
    being shifted; results stay within the nominal range.
  - Added integer overloads (8 bit sRGB <-> 16 bit DICOM CIELab) that
    round and clamp.
  - 8 bit round trip through DICOM CIELab is exact for all 16.7 million
    RGB triples (new EF_Slow test); test vectors are shared with PixelMed.
  Thanks to Andrey Fedorov, David Clunie and Michael Halle for the
  analysis in dcmqi issue #563.
  Affects: dcmiod/include/dcmtk/dcmiod/cielabutil.h
           dcmiod/libsrc/cielabutil.cc
           dcmiod/tests/tcielabutil.cc
           dcmiod/tests/tests.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.20 (eichelberg)

- Fixed commit #6a6336a5b on big endian:
  The fix for DCMTK issue #1285 did not work correctly on big endian CPUs
  because the re-ordering from color-by-plane to color-by-pixel took place
  before the byte order was correctly swapped. This is now fixed.
  Affects: dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcodece.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.19 (eichelberg)

- Fixed minor warning.
  Affects: dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcodece.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.18 (eichelberg)

- Added workaround option to the JPEG decoder:
  Added a new command line option --workaround-planar that will cause the
  JPEG decoder to fix incorrectly encoded color multiframe issues
  affected by DCMTK's issue #1285 by re-sorting color components after
  decompression.
  Affects: dcmjpeg/apps/dcmdjpeg.cc
           dcmjpeg/docs/dcmdjpeg.man
           dcmjpeg/include/dcmtk/dcmjpeg/djcodecd.h
           dcmjpeg/include/dcmtk/dcmjpeg/djcparam.h
           dcmjpeg/include/dcmtk/dcmjpeg/djdecode.h
           dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcodecd.cc
           dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcparam.cc
           dcmjpeg/libsrc/djdecode.cc
           dcmjpeg/libsrc/djencode.cc

- Fixed JPEG compression of color multiframe images:
  Fixed JPEG compression of color multiframe images that have a color-by-plane
  encoding, i.e. Planar Configuration (0028,0006) has a value of 1.
  When re-sorting color componentes to color-by-pixel encoding, as required
  by the JPEG encoder, the implementation failed to take into account that
  each frame must be handled separately. This caused color components to
  be mixed up, resulting in a compressed image with incorrect colors.
  Thanks to Christian Wetzel for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1285.
  Affects: dcmjpeg/include/dcmtk/dcmjpeg/djcodece.h
           dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcodece.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.14 (onken)

- Rebuild dependencies.
  Affects: dcmqrdb/tests/Makefile.dep

**** Changes from 2026.09.13 (onken)

- Fixed prefix match in QR index quota eviction:
  deleteOldestStudy() and deleteOldestImages() compared Study Instance
  UIDs with strncmp() over the length of the selected UID, i.e. by
  prefix, while matchStudyUIDInStudyDesc() has always used strcmp().
  If one Study Instance UID was a textual prefix of another - the
  normal case for UIDs ending in an unpadded counter - evicting the
  shorter one silently deleted the other study as well. Both places
  now require an exact match.
  Thanks to Abhinav Agarwal for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1284.
  Added:   dcmqrdb/tests/tquota.cc
  Affects: dcmqrdb/libsrc/dcmqrdbi.cc
           dcmqrdb/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmqrdb/tests/Makefile.in
           dcmqrdb/tests/tests.cc

- Fixed read-only storage area bypass in dcmqrscp:
  DcmQueryRetrieveSCP::dispatch() switched on the DIMSE command field
  alone, so a C-STORE request sent on the accepted Verification
  presentation context bypassed the refusal of all storage contexts
  that enforces "Access R". The resulting stores also triggered the
  quota mechanism, deleting objects already stored in that area.
  - dispatch() now rejects any command that is not defined for the
    abstract syntax of its presentation context, and aborts
  - storeSCP() refuses a store to a non-writable area with 0x0124, so
    the access mode no longer depends on negotiation alone
  Thanks to Abhinav Agarwal for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1283.
  Added:   dcmqrdb/tests/tdispatch.cc
  Affects: dcmqrdb/include/dcmtk/dcmqrdb/dcmqrsrv.h
           dcmqrdb/libsrc/dcmqrsrv.cc
           dcmqrdb/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmqrdb/tests/Makefile.in
           dcmqrdb/tests/tests.cc

- Fixed out-of-bounds read in DUL_NextPDV():
  When a P-DATA-TF PDU carried multiple PDVs of unequal length,
  DUL_NextPDV() advanced the persistent pdvPointer by "4 + pdvLength"
  using the next PDV's length instead of the length of the PDV just
  traversed. This causes an out-of-bounds read and a crash of the
  receiving SCP (remote, unauthenticated DoS). Assign the already-computed
  correct address instead.
  Thanks to Zhanglinghang for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1282.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dul.cc

**** Changes from 2026.09.11 (onken)

- Updated Makefile dependencies.
  Affects: dcmfg/tests/Makefile.dep

- Validate buffer length in extractBinaryFrames:
  DcmIODUtil::extractBinaryFrames() now takes the number of bytes
  available in the pixel data buffer and verifies it is large enough
  for the requested frames before copying, returning
  IOD_EC_InvalidPixelData otherwise. Previously every caller had to
  check this externally, which the ConcatenationLoader failed to do
  (heap over-read). Callers in dcmseg and dcmfg pass the length; the
  dcmfg binary path drops its now-redundant inline check.
  Affects: dcmfg/libsrc/concatenationloader.cc
           dcmiod/include/dcmtk/dcmiod/iodutil.h
           dcmiod/libsrc/iodutil.cc
           dcmseg/libsrc/segdoc.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tutils.cc

- Fixed heap over-read in ConcatenationLoader:
  extractFrames() and extractBinaryFrames() copied pixel data
  frame-by-frame using the NumberOfFrames tag without checking that
  the Pixel Data element actually holds that many frames, causing a
  heap over-read (DoS or information disclosure) on crafted objects.
  Both paths now verify the buffer length before copying and reject
  undersized data. computeBytesPerFrame() now computes in size_t so
  the Rows*Columns*BitsAllocated product cannot overflow. Added a
  regression test.
  Thanks to Tristan for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1281.
  Affects: dcmfg/libsrc/concatenationloader.cc
           dcmfg/tests/t_concatenation_loader.cc
           dcmfg/tests/tests.cc

- Fixed View Code Sequence macro reading/writing:
  MandatoryViewAndSliceProgressionDirectionMacro::read() called
  IODComponent::read() last with clearOldData enabled, which (since
  clearData() became virtual) deleted the View Code Sequence and View
  Modifier Code Sequence values that had just been read. Reading now
  follows the common pattern: clear first, then read.
  Also, the View Modifier Code Sequence was read from the wrong
  location (the View Code Sequence itself, also using that sequence's
  rule) and written to the top level of the macro; per DICOM part 3 it
  is nested within the single item of the View Code Sequence. Read and
  write now use that item. Added a regression test.
  Thanks to Piotr Batko for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1280.
  Affects: dcmiod/libsrc/iodmacro.cc
           dcmiod/tests/tests.cc
           dcmiod/tests/tmacro.cc

**** Changes from 2026.08.24 (onken)

- Fixed 32-bit overflow in DcmElement::changeValue():
  The append branch allocated getLengthField() + num bytes in 32-bit
  arithmetic, which can wrap and undersize the buffer that the following
  memcpy then overruns. Reject the operation with
  EC_ElemLengthExceeds32BitField when the combined length would exceed
  the 32-bit value-length limit.
  Thanks to Kamal Sentassi (S9S Security Electronic Service) for the
  report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1278.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcelem.cc

- Fixed User Identity sub-item parser desync:
  UserIdentityNegotiationSubItemRQ::parseFromBuffer() only added the
  secondary-field length to the returned bytesRead for the
  USERNAME+PASSWORD identity type. For any other identity type with a
  non-zero secondary field, bytesRead was short by that length, so the
  caller re-parsed the trailing bytes as a bogus following User-Info
  sub-item. Account for the secondary field in bytesRead unconditionally.
  Added a regression test.
  Thanks to Kamal Sentassi (S9S Security Electronic Service) for the
  report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1277.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dcuserid.cc
           dcmnet/tests/tests.cc
           dcmnet/tests/tparseassoc.cc

**** Changes from 2026.08.21 (onken)

- Fixed setReferencedFrameNumber().
  Affects: dcmiod/libsrc/iodmacro.cc
           dcmiod/tests/Makefile.dep
