**** Changes from 2026.06.21 (onken)

- Avoid warning in readPDU() overflow guard:
  Compute the PDU buffer size with OFStandard::safeAdd() instead of
  comparing nextPDULength against size_t(-1) - 100, which is always false
  on LLP64 platforms (e.g. 64-bit Windows) and therefore warns.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dulfsm.cc

**** Changes from 2026.06.19 (onken)

- Regenerated Makefile dependencies.
  Affects: dcmsr/libsrc/Makefile.dep

- Use OFStandard::strlcpy instead of strncpy():
  Use OFStandard::strlcpy instead of strncpy() ensuring resulting string
  is always NUL-terminated.
  Thanks to Arash Ale Ebrahim for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1232.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dimcmd.cc

- Fix OOB read in sanitizeFilename() on NUL bytes:
  The OFString overload of OFStandard::sanitizeFilename() iterates by
  length(), so it also visits embedded NUL bytes (which OFString and
  DcmByteString preserve). The existing guard lets NUL bytes pass through,
  leading to a negative out of bounds array lookup in sanitized_filename_charset.
  Dropping the "c != 0" guard makes a NUL be treated as a control
  character and replaced with '_', matching the intent of the original
  code and the behaviour of the char* overload. A regression test in
  tofstd.cc covers the embedded-NUL case and the path-separator,
  high-byte and empty-string cases.
  Thanks to Arash Ale Ebrahim for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1231.
  Affects: ofstd/libsrc/ofstd.cc
           ofstd/tests/tests.cc
           ofstd/tests/tofstd.cc

- Fix memory leak on duplicate User Ident. sub-items:
  parseUserInfo() stored each parsed User Identity Negotiation sub-item
  (item type 0x58) in the single userInfo->usrIdent pointer. A second
  sub-item in the same A-ASSOCIATE-RQ silently overwrote the first with no
  free, and destroyUserInformationLists() can only release whichever
  pointer is stored last, so every earlier allocation leaked permanently.
  An unauthenticated peer could pack many sub-items into a single PDU
  (bounded only by dcmAssociatePDUSizeLimit) and reconnect repeatedly to
  exhaust server memory, affecting every SCP that calls
  ASC_receiveAssociation (probably all DCMTK SCP tools).
  DICOM permits this sub-item at most once per association, so a duplicate
  is now rejected as an illegal PDU. A regression test in tparseassoc.cc
  crafts an A-ASSOCIATE-RQ with two such sub-items and checks that parsing
  is rejected and the error-path cleanup clears the stored pointer.
  Thanks to Arash Ale Ebrahim for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1230.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dulparse.cc
           dcmnet/tests/tests.cc
           dcmnet/tests/tparseassoc.cc

