**** Changes from 2026.06.19 (onken)

- Replaced some old-style casts by OF... casts.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/scu.cc
           dcmnet/tests/tscuscp.cc

- Fix potent. heap overflow in DB_DuplicateElement:
  Use a size_t cast (not int) for the malloc size so large ValueLength
  values can no longer truncate/sign-flip into an undersized buffer.
  Also run memset/memcpy only after the NULL check, avoiding a crash
  when the allocation fails.
  Thanks to Dominik Blain for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1229.
  Affects: dcmqrdb/libsrc/dcmqrdbi.cc

- Fix potential heap overflow:
  Fix potential heap overflow that could occur if the safety margin
  of 100 bytes added to the expected PDU length goes beyond the size of
  int, leading (through the sign flipping) to very large allocations.
  The fix ensures that the buffer length (including safety margin) works
  and if larger than max PDU size (~4 GB), rejects the PDU.
  Thanks to Dominik Blain for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1228.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dulfsm.cc

- Make buffer big enough to fit DNS resolve result:
  An attacker controlling a PTR DNS record could overflow a 260-byte stack
  buffer on every incoming DICOM TCP connection (port 104).Remote,
  unauthenticated.
  The fix ensures the buffer is large enough and could be allocated
  successfully.
  Thanks to Dominik Blain for the report.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1227.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dul.cc

