**** Changes from 2026.06.10 (onken)

- Fix OOB read in JPEG-LS gradient quantization:
  QuantizeGratient(Di) returns *(_pquant + Di) where _pquant points
  into the middle of a 2*RANGE entry table; valid indices are
  [-RANGE, RANGE-1]. The out-of-range guard in DoLine used a strict
  '> RANGE_UPPER', letting a gradient of exactly RANGE through to
  QuantizeGratient(RANGE), which reads _rgquant[2*RANGE] one past the
  end. Use '>= RANGE_UPPER' so the exclusive upper bound matches the
  valid index range; the lower bound stays strict because -RANGE is a
  valid index.
  The scalar DoLine(SAMPLE*) path had this guard; the interleaved
  DoLine(Triplet<SAMPLE>*) path (ILV_SAMPLE colour images) did not and
  called QuantizeGratient on its nine per-component gradients with no
  bounds check, so a crafted colour stream hit the same OOB. Add the
  matching guard there too. The OOB is reachable whenever the declared
  MAXVAL is an exact power of two: then RANGE_UPPER == MAXVAL and
  clamped samples 0..MAXVAL can differ by exactly RANGE_UPPER.
  Real images keep gradients within [-(RANGE-1), RANGE-1], so only
  corrupt data is affected and it is rejected as InvalidCompressedData
  as before.
  Thanks to Yiyi Wang for the report and analysis.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1223.
  Affects: dcmjpls/libcharls/scan.h

**** Changes from 2026.06.05 (eichelberg)

- Fixed previous commit.
  Affects: dcmimage/libsrc/CMakeLists.txt

- Fixed DCMTK_TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES call:
  Fixed DCMTK_TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES call, which must not contain the PRIVATE
  keyword in this place; this interferes with the DBUILD_SINGLE_SHARED_LIBRARY
  option.
  Affects: CMake/dcmtkAfterModules.cmake
           dcmimage/libsrc/CMakeLists.txt

- Enable CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE when needed:
  Set CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE to ON if we are building shared libraries.
  This will cause CMake to add the compiler flag for position independent code.
  In most cases CMake does this automatically, but in some cases (such as
  the BUILD_SINGLE_SHARED_LIBRARY option) it does not.
  Affects: CMake/dcmtkPrepare.cmake

- Disable CMake code depending on BUILD_APPS:
  Disable some CMake code that should not be executed if BUILD_APPS is false.
  Affects: dcmdata/tests/CMakeLists.txt

**** Changes from 2026.06.05 (onken)

- Fix data race on SCP pool run mode:
  DcmBaseSCPPool::m_runMode was guarded by m_criticalSection in
  stopAfterCurrentAssociations()/finishListening() but read and written
  unlocked in the destructor and listen(), so the listen loop's
  run-mode check raced the stop request (flagged by ThreadSanitizer).
  Route the unguarded accesses through new getRunMode()/setRunMode()
  accessors that take m_criticalSection. Benign (worst case one extra
  listen iteration), but now race-free.
  Affects: dcmnet/include/dcmtk/dcmnet/scppool.h
           dcmnet/libsrc/scppool.cc

- Fix data race in DUL FSM initialization:
  DUL_InitializeNetwork() lazily fills the global FSM StateTable
  (action-function pointers) under an unsynchronized networkInitialized
  flag. With concurrent associations (SCP pool plus several SCUs) one
  thread could read a StateTable entry while another still wrote it, so
  the state machine dispatched through a half-set pointer and the TLS
  handshake failed intermittently. ThreadSanitizer confirmed the race.
  Serialize the init with a mutex, taken on every call so later callers
  synchronize with the initializing thread. Verified with TSan.
  Affects: dcmnet/libsrc/dul.cc

**** Changes from 2026.06.03 (onken)

- Use an unencrypted key in the TLS SCU/SCP tests:
  It looks like a custom OpenSSL 3.5.0 on one nightly build machine
  (Debian Trixie) cannot decode the encrypted PKCS#8 test key (DECODER
  routines::unsupported, regardless of cipher), so the SCP has no key and
  every handshake fails with "no suitable signature algorithm". The
  affected tests check TLS communication, not encrypted-key loading.
  This commit tries to fix the poblem by the key unencrypted (same
  keypair, cert unchanged) and drop the password handling.
  Affects: dcmtls/tests/tscuscptls.cc

**** Changes from 2026.06.02 (onken)

- Fixed memory leaks in some apps:
  Until now, not all DCMTK apps freed their allocated heap memory on exit,
  relying instead on the operating system to reclaim it. While that is
  usually acceptable, it makes the apps more cumbersome to use for testing
  library changes with memory leak detection tools.
  This commit tries to fix as many leaks as could be found but its
  possible that some are still left and will be fixed in the future
  as they are revealed.
  Affects: dcmdata/apps/Makefile.dep
           dcmdata/apps/dcmcrle.cc
