**** Changes from 2026.06.01 (onken)

- Encrypt dcmtls key with AES-256-CBC inst. of 3DES:
  The private key embedded in tscuscptls.cc was 3DES-encrypted. On modern
  OpenSSL builds without the legacy provider (e.g. Debian trixie) the key
  fails to load (DECODER routines::unsupported), leaving the SCP without a
  usable key, so dcmtls_scp_pool_tls/dcmtls_scp_tls fail every handshake with
  "no suitable signature algorithm". Re-encrypted the same key with
  AES-256-CBC (default provider everywhere); certificate and keypair
  unchanged.
  Affects: dcmtls/tests/tscuscptls.cc

