**** Changes from 2026.05.07 (onken)

- Avoid shift of negative char in DcmHashDict::hash:
  When privCreator contains a byte with the high bit set, *privCreator
  (a plain char, signed on most targets) sign-extends to a negative int,
  and shifting a negative int is undefined behavior per the C/C++
  standard. Cast through unsigned char first so the shift is well
  defined and the per-byte XOR pattern matches the original intent.
  Detected by UBSan during fuzz testing.
  Thanks to GitHub user MarkLee131 for the report and fix.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dchashdi.cc

