- Only build error message string when needed:
  Defer DcmTag(tagKey).getTagName() and the OFOStringStream build in
  DcmIODUtil::checkElementValue() to the error branch.  On the common
  success path these were constructed unconditionally and then
  discarded, which showed up in profiles of read-heavy workloads.
  Also tighten the unknown-error fallback: explicitly keep only
  EC_InvalidCharacter, EC_ValueRepresentationViolated,
  EC_ValueMultiplicityViolated, and EC_MaximumLengthViolated as
  reportable validation errors; everything else from checkValue() is
  downgraded to EC_Normal (was previously an INTERNAL ERROR log entry
  that reset the result to EC_Normal anyway).
  Affects: dcmiod/libsrc/iodutil.cc

- Thread-safe FGFactory; remove redundant FG lock:
  Protect FGFactory::instance() with an OFMutex and double-checked
  locking so concurrent first-time access cannot race on construction.
  The mutex is declared at class-static scope (not function-local) so
  that its initialization is guaranteed before any user thread exists
  (C++98 function-local static initialization is not thread-safe, and
  that applies to the mutex itself).
  Drop the mutex around m_frameResultGroups writes in
  FGInterface::ThreadedFGReader::run(): each worker writes to its own
  non-overlapping frame-number slot, so no synchronization is needed on
  the store.  The previous "kept for safety" comment is misleading --
  the partition is a fixed invariant of the scheduler, not a
  coincidence.
  Affects: dcmfg/include/dcmtk/dcmfg/fgfact.h
           dcmfg/libsrc/fgfact.cc
           dcmfg/libsrc/fginterface.cc

- Check all pixel values have segment:
  For LABELMAP segmentations, every pixel value in the pixel data must
  be described by a Segment Sequence item (Sup 243, C.8.20.2.3.3).
  Extend DcmSegmentation::check() to iterate all pixels across all
  frames and fail the check when a pixel value has no corresponding
  segment (or the segment slot is NULL).
  Existing tests updated to satisfy the new invariant.
  Affects: dcmseg/libsrc/segdoc.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tbigdim.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tlabelmap.cc

- No CIE Lab Color Rec.Value for PALETTE segs:
  Per Sup 243, the Recommended Display CIELab Value shall not be
  present on a segment item when Segmentation Type is LABELMAP and
  Photometric Interpretation is PALETTE COLOR.  On write, strip the
  attribute from the segment item in that case.
  Affects: dcmseg/libsrc/segdoc.cc

- Segment management now uses vector instead of map:
  DcmSegmentation::m_Segments was an OFMap<Uint16, DcmSegment*> — frame
  numbers are dense, so lookup by segment number is now an O(1)
  OFVector index.  The public API (getSegment(), addSegment(), etc.)
  is preserved; a compat layer provides map-style access for callers
  that still expect it.
  Added tsegments.cc covering add/get, segment-number lookups, many-
  segment scaling, the compat layer, sparse labelmap handling, and
  compat-caching behaviour.
  Added:   dcmseg/tests/tsegments.cc
  Affects: dcmfg/libsrc/fginterface.cc
           dcmseg/include/dcmtk/dcmseg/segdoc.h
           dcmseg/libsrc/segdoc.cc
           dcmseg/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmseg/tests/tbigdim.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tests.cc

- Replace OFMap with OFVector in FG interface class:
  FGInterface::m_perFrame used OFMap<Uint32, FunctionalGroups*> backed
  by OFList, making every per-frame lookup O(n).  Since frame numbers
  are dense 0..N-1, an OFVector indexed by frame number gives O(1)
  access.  Also fixes a bug in check() that caused a slow down.
  Added tests for FGInterface that exercise the public API.
  Also fix a per-frame FG write bug exposed by the switch:
  writePerFrameFGSequential() used the vector index as the DICOM
  sequence item position. With 1-based frame numbers the NULL slot at
  index 0 was skipped, but findOrCreateSequenceItem() still created an
  empty item, producing N+1 sequence items. Use a separate counter that
  only increments for non-NULL entries.
  Added:   dcmfg/tests/t_fginterface.cc
  Affects: dcmfg/include/dcmtk/dcmfg/fginterface.h
           dcmfg/libsrc/fginterface.cc
           dcmfg/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmfg/tests/tests.cc
  Removed: dcmseg/tests/tpacking.cc

- Optimize binary frame extraction:
  Add fast path in case frames are byte-aligned.
  For the slow path work byte-wise and don't access variables more
  often then necessary.
  Added roundtrip test (dcmseg_extractBinaryFrames) covering the fast
  and slow paths.
  Affects: dcmiod/libsrc/iodutil.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tests.cc
           dcmseg/tests/tutils.cc

- dcmiod: static per-class default IODRules (cow):
  Every IODComponent subclass now lazily initializes a static
  OFshared_ptr<IODRules> on first instantiation (guarded by a per-class
  OFMutex) and shares it across all instances via m_Rules. Mutation
  (makeOptional, getRules()) triggers copy-on-write via ensureOwnRules().
  The DcmIODCommon shared-container pattern (m_ExternalRules) is preserved:
  resetRules() copies rules into the external container in that case.
  Each affected .cc file carries a comment explaining why the shared
  OFshared_ptr<IODRules> and its OFMutex must live at namespace scope:
  in C++98 the initialization of function-local statics is not
  thread-safe (and that applies to the OFMutex itself), so a Meyers-
  singleton rewrite would break the pattern. The comment is intended to
  prevent future "cleanup" regressions.
  Added:   dcmiod/tests/tstaticrules.cc
  Affects: dcmfg/libsrc/fgrealworldvaluemapping.cc
           dcmiod/include/dcmtk/dcmiod/modbase.h
           dcmiod/libsrc/iodcontentitemmacro.cc
           dcmiod/libsrc/iodmacro.cc
