**** Changes from 2026.04.10 (onken)

- Conditions: Fixed 64-bit int parsing and ranges:
  The checkIntegerValidity() function in MdfDatasetManager had several issues:
    1. Replaced sscanf() with OFSstringstream for portable 64-bit integer parsing.
       The sscanf() approach with platform-specific format specifiers (%lu, %llu,
       PRIu64) was unreliable on 32-bit platforms.
    2. Fixed OFnumeric_limits<T>::max to OFnumeric_limits<T>::max() (added
       parentheses), since max() is a function, not a variable.
    3. Fixed signed integer overflow bug: the original code used limitValue++
       for negative values, which caused undefined behavior when limitValue was
       OFnumeric_limits<Sint64>::max() (overflow to min value). Now properly
       checks against both min() and max() values.
    Also adds missing include for OFIStringStream.
    The tests now use full 64-bit values (exceeding 32-bit range) for UV, SV,
    and OV VRs to properly exercise 64-bit integer handling on both 32-bit and
    64-bit platforms.
  Affects: dcmdata/apps/mdfdsman.cc
           dcmdata/tests/tcond.cc

**** Changes from 2026.04.09 (onken)

- Fixed BE pixel data in ConcatenationCreator:
  Fixed a bug where ConcatenationCreator wrote the pixel data with wrong
  byte ordering on Big Endian machines for 16 bit data.
  ConcatenationCreator::writeNextInstance() always used createUint8Array()
  for destination pixel data, even for 16-bit (OW) data. This set the
  internal currentVR to EVR_OB. The subsequent setVR(EVR_OW) only changed
  the tag VR, not currentVR. During serialization, DcmPolymorphOBOW::write()
  detected tag VR OW with currentVR OB and assumed little endian byte order,
  which is correct for actual OB data but wrong when the buffer contains
  native byte order 16-bit words. On big endian systems this caused pixel
  values to be written without byte swap, resulting in corrupted pixel data
  in concatenation instances (e.g. dcmect_roundtrip test failure on s390x).
  Fixed by using createUint16Array() for OW pixel data, which correctly
  sets currentVR to EVR_OW and ensures proper byte order handling.
  This closes DCMTK Bug #1201.
  Affects: dcmfg/libsrc/concatenationcreator.cc

**** Changes from 2026.04.08 (eichelberg)

- Fixed use of sscanf() with 64-bit int.
  Affects: dcmdata/apps/mdfdsman.cc

- Fixed Windows DLL build with STL enabled.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcdocdec.cc

**** Changes from 2026.04.07 (onken)

- Lower nesting level depth test for Windows:
  The test can fail on Windows since nesting level was to 200, which might
  exceed the max 1 MB stack memory on Windows.  So the test is adapted to
  be (still) above the default of 64 but not so high that it could exceed
  maximum stack memory.
  Affects: dcmdata/tests/tnesting.cc

**** Changes from 2026.04.07 (xu)

- Add --process-if option to dcmodify:
  Add conditional execution of modifications via the new -iff/--process-if
  option. Conditions support existence checks (E, !), equality (=, !=) and
  ordering (<, <=, >, >=) operators. Multiple conditions are combined with
  logical AND.
  Condition checking covers all DICOM VR categories:
  - Numeric VRs (US, SS, UL, SL, UV, SV, FL, FD) via DcmElement::compare()
  - String VRs (CS, LO, PN, DA, UI, etc.) via lexicographic comparison
  - Binary VRs (OB, OW, UN) via hex representation
  - Other numeric VRs (OL, OV, OF, OD) via their numeric parent class
    comparison
  - AT (Attribute Tag) as string
  Includes bug fixes found during test development:
  - Fix comparison error silently discarded: return value from
    checkNumberCondition() was overwritten by
    evaluateCompareResult(), causing all conditions to appear as "equal"
    when comparison failed.
  - Fix checkIntegerValidity() rejecting all IS values:
    getValueWidth() returns sizeof(char) for IS which matched no
    integer width check.
  - Route UN through numeric path instead of string path:
    getString() returns raw binary data for DcmOtherByteOtherWord, making
    the string path unusable for value comparisons.
  - Skip decimal normalization for OB/OW/UN in createCompareElement():
    these VRs use hex format for putString().
  Adds unit tests (tcond.cc) and updates the dcmodify man page that
  documents details of the new feature.
  Added:   dcmdata/tests/tcond.cc
  Affects: dcmdata/apps/Makefile.dep
           dcmdata/apps/mdfconen.cc
           dcmdata/apps/mdfconen.h
           dcmdata/apps/mdfdsman.cc
           dcmdata/apps/mdfdsman.h
           dcmdata/docs/dcmodify.man
           dcmdata/include/dcmtk/dcmdata/dcerror.h
           dcmdata/libsrc/dcerror.cc
           dcmdata/tests/CMakeLists.txt
           dcmdata/tests/Makefile.dep
           dcmdata/tests/Makefile.in
           dcmdata/tests/tests.cc

