**** Changes from 2026.04.04 (eichelberg)

- Fixed assertion failure in JPEG-LS export:
  Fixed an assertion failure that could occur in debug mode when dcm2img was
  instructed to convert an image with signed representation to JPEG-LS
  in 'true lossless' mode.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1188.
  Affects: dcmimgle/include/dcmtk/dcmimgle/diimage.h
           dcmjpls/libsrc/dipijpls.cc

**** Changes from 2026.03.29 (eichelberg)

- Fixed race condition in file path resolution:
  Fixed a time-of-check-to-time-of-use race condition in
  DcmJSONReader::loadBulkdataFile() that could be used by a malicious
  attacker to replace the input directory with a symbolic link pointing
  somewhere else, thus causing a file outside the permitted path
  to be read.
  Thanks to the IN-CYPHER OSS Security Team for the report, detailed
  analysis, proof of concept and proposed fix.
  This closes DCMTK Bug #1198.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

- Fixed uninitialized memory read in JSON parser:
  Fixed uninitialized memory read in JSMN Token Array
  that could cause undefined behavior when reading a malformed JSON file.
  Thanks to the IN-CYPHER OSS Security Team for the report, detailed
  analysis, proof of concept and proposed fix.
  This closes DCMTK Bug #1197.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

**** Changes from 2026.03.28 (eichelberg)

- Fixed out-of-bound read in JSON parser:
  Fixed a segmentation fault caused by an out-of-bound heap
  read access in DcmJSONReader::getTokenContent() when reading
  malformed JSON data.
  Thanks to the IN-CYPHER OSS Security Team for the report, detailed
  analysis, proof of concept and proposed fix.
  This closes DCMTK Bug #1193.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

