**** Changes from 2026.03.13 (riesmeier)

- Fixed Base64 encoding in Native DICOM Model:
  Fixed byte ordering of Base64 encoded <InlineBinary> data in Native
  DICOM Model. The byte ordering is now little endian (instead of big
  endian) and, therefore, consistent with the Base64 encoding of the
  DICOM JSON Model.
  The byte ordering of Base64 encoded OW data in the DCMTK-specific XML
  format is still big endian. And that's also the byte ordering that is
  expected by xml2dcm (and the underlying DcmXMLParseHelper class). Added
  notes to the manpages of dcm2xml and xml2dcm about the byte ordering.
  Also simplified the internal byte swapping in case the byte ordering
  needs to be changed.
  Affects: dcmdata/docs/dcm2xml.man
           dcmdata/docs/xml2dcm.man
           dcmdata/include/dcmtk/dcmdata/dcelem.h
