**** Changes from 2026.03.10 (riesmeier)

- Fixed infinite loop in JPEG segment parser:
  Fixed an infinite loop in the JPEG segment parser that occurred when
  parsing a JPEG data stream with a TEM marker (0xFF01). This Temporary
  Marker is a special, parameterless marker that is mainly used for
  non-progressive JPEG images with arithmetic coding.
  Thanks to the IN-CYPHER OSS Security Team for the report, detailed
  analysis, proof of concept and proposed fix.
  This closes DCMTK Bug #1190.
  Affects: dcmjpeg/libsrc/djcodecd.cc

- Added method hasConstraintChecker():
  Added method hasConstraintChecker() to the DSRDocumentSubTree class,
  which checks whether a constraint checker is defined, i.e. a class that
  ensures that the "relationship content constraints" are respected, e.g.
  according to DICOM PS3.3.
  Affects: dcmsr/include/dcmtk/dcmsr/dsrdocst.h
           dcmsr/libsrc/dsrdocst.cc
           dcmsr/libsrc/dsrdoctr.cc
