**** Changes from 2026.03.09 (riesmeier)

- Fixed memory leaks when parsing invalid JSON data:
  Fixed two memory leaks that occurred when parsing invalid JSON data.
  These issues have been found with an address sanitizer.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

- Report an error if Base64 data cannot be decoded:
  Report a message to the logger and return with an error if Base64 input
  data cannot be decoded. This is true for the DCMTK-specific XML format
  and the DICOM JSON Model. Before, decoding failures were ignored.
  Affects: dcmdata/libdcxml/xml2dcm.cc
           dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

- Set resulting pointer to NULL in case of error:
  Made sure that the resulting pointer returned by decodeBase64() is set
  to NULL if an error occurred, e.g. not enough data in the input string.
  Affects: ofstd/include/dcmtk/ofstd/ofstd.h
           ofstd/libsrc/ofstd.cc

- Fixed double-free vulnerability in JSON reader:
  Fixed a deletion of an invalid pointer when reading invalid Base64 data
  from a JSON file. The error returned by OFStandard::decodeBase64() was
  ignored.
  Thanks to the IN-CYPHER OSS Security Team for the report, detailed
  analysis and proof of concept.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcjsonrd.cc

