**** Changes from 2026.02.05 (riesmeier)

- Enhanced support for absence of time zone info:
  The class OFTime now clearly distinguishes between the presence and
  absence of time zone information. Before, OFTime did not always know
  whether time zone information was available or not, since internally
  the value "0" was used for both UTC and unknown/absent time zone
  information.
  Please note that OFTime::getISOFormattedTime() no longer adds "+0000"
  (for UTC) to the output string, if the time zone is unspecified. If you
  want to use the local time zone, you can now specify this easily by
  calling OFTime::setLocalTimeZone().
  This feature also has an impact on OFDateTime, DcmTime and DcmDateTime.
  This closes DCMTK Feature #1127.
  Affects: dcmdata/include/dcmtk/dcmdata/dcvrtm.h
           ofstd/include/dcmtk/ofstd/ofdatime.h
           ofstd/include/dcmtk/ofstd/oftime.h
           ofstd/libsrc/oftime.cc
           ofstd/tests/tofdatim.cc

