  Affects: dcmdata/docs/json2dcm.man

**** Changes from 2026.02.03 (xu)

- Implemented DICOM CP 2518 in dcm2json and json2dcm:
  The dcm2json and json2dcm tools now correctly handle Specific Character Set
  (0008,0005) when converting between DICOM and JSON. When converting to JSON,
  by default the value of Specific Character Set will be retained even though
  the JSON dataset itself is expressed in UTF-8. When converting from JSON to
  DICOM and encountering a Specific Character Set other than ISO_IR 192,
  json2dcm will attempt to convert the character set back to its original form.
  This will fail if multiple character sets were in use in parallel
  (e.g. for the Japanese language). In this case, the option --charset-utf8
  allows to keep the dataset in UTF-8 encoding.
  This closes DCMTK issue #1181.
  Affects: dcmdata/apps/dcm2json.cc
           dcmdata/apps/json2dcm.cc
           dcmdata/docs/dcm2json.man
           dcmdata/docs/json2dcm.man

