**** Changes from 2026.01.29 (riesmeier)

- Fixed issue with unexpected PixelDataProviderURL:
  Fixed an issue when trying to convert an uncompressed DICOM image to
  another uncompressed transfer syntax, e.g. ILE to ELE, and the data set
  contains a PixelDataProviderURL element, which does not comply with the
  DICOM standard. Instead of aborting the conversion process with an error,
  now a warning message is printed.
  However, when both PixelDataProviderURL and PixelData are present in a
  data set that is encoded with one of the two JPIP transfer syntaxes, an
  error message is printed and the conversion is aborted.
  Also improved the output of log messages for some cases.
  Thanks to Sjors Gielen <sjors@sjorsgielen.nl> for the original report
  and a sample file that demonstrates the problem.
  Affects: dcmdata/libsrc/dcdatset.cc

